  "summary": "Malicious code in prettier-logger (npm)",
  "details": "A trojanized npm package posing as a colorized logger. On require(), it collects the OS, IP address, and username, then installs a hardcoded attacker SSH ed25519 public key into ~/.ssh/authorized_keys on Linux for persistent backdoor access. It recursively walks the entire filesystem (/, C:\\, /Users) searching for.env and config.json files, reads their contents, and POSTs them to api[.]fivefingerz[.]dev under the /api/validate/files, /api/validate/system-info, and /api/validate/project-env endpoints. The package manifest impersonates an author named Luke Pammant.",
